<title>INDIA: Indian soymeal prices rise on export demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soymeal prices rise on export demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean and soyoil prices were firm on decreased arrivals on Wednesday. Soybean prices were up by 100-150 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices continued firm on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $280 per tonne ready delivery and was $276-277 per tonne November, December and January shipment in new season.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $125 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,250 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,200-4,225 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
